From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: offload VLAN-aware DSA routing

VLAN-aware vsc73xx-8021q bridges carry the customer VID directly on
the conduit. Resolve the rule's VLAN or the access port's PVID instead
of rejecting filtering ports or pushing an extra internal DSA tag.
Validate bridge protocol, forwarding state and VLAN membership.

Give each conduit/VID a referenced L3 interface for ingress routing
and egress MAC rewriting, bind its router MAC before publishing either
direction, and use the VLAN VSI rather than the shared port identity.
Check the source L3 interface in hardware so an existing five-tuple
cannot bypass policy when received from another VLAN.

Drain installed flows on DSA bridge VLAN, PVID, filtering, STP, MAC and
link changes. Serialize installation with these notifications using a
non-blocking RTNL acquisition: teardown may flush the offload workqueue
while holding RTNL, so waiting for it here would deadlock.

Clear recycled VLAN L3 rows and verify shared slots retain compatible
CPU tag handling. VLAN-unaware internal tags retain their original
single-tag behavior; stacked customer and internal tags stay rejected.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
